Unpack the file wang1200wps.zip into your home directory:

	Double-click on wang1200wps.zip (Open), then drag-n-drop
	"wang1200wps" into your home directory.

	Double-click on "wang1200wps" from your home directory,
	then double-click on INSTALL to setup files.

Setup Environment Variables:

	(e.g. Windows 7) Right click on "My Computer" and select
	...

	Add the following:

		WANG1200_HOST - set to hostname of Wang1200 server

		WANG1200_PORT - set to port number used by Wang1200 server

	Ensure that "Path" contains the Java home and command directories,
	such that typing the command "java" in a command prompt window
	works. This should be part of normal Java install/setup.

Create a shortcut on your Desktop:

	Right-click on your Desktop, select "New"->"Shortcut".

	Enter path to Wang1200.bat, for example:

		C:\Users\Owner\wang1200wps\Wang1200.bat

	Click "Next"

	Change name is desired, should default to "Wang1200".

	Click "Finish"

	Right-click on new shortcut, select "Properties".

	Click on "Change Icon", browse to C:\Users\Owner\wang1200wps\icons
	and select "wang1200-48x48.ico", click "OK" as needed.


NOTE: Requires Java. The run script (batch file) expects the command "java"
to work, specifically that "java -jar file" will invoke the java code in
the "jar" file named "file". Oracle/Sun Java JRE does this. Unknown if
other Java runtimes use the same command syntax. Edit "Wang1200.bat" as
needed to change command syntax.
